Extends patch 0080's existing backdrop cache + patch 0126's wave-30
thrashing-detect with a CORRECTNESS-PRESERVING natural-origin output
cache for the generic-loop scrolltypes (BK_PARALLAX / BK_FOLLOWFG /
BK_FASTLEFT / BK_FIXED). Sub-decomposes the cache key per wave-31
contract: removes parscroll_x/y; cached output stays valid as long as
map / scrolltype / backdrop_id / format / window-dim don't change. On
hit, parscroll is applied as a SRC OFFSET in the cache→window blit
instead of being part of the key.

**Critical interpretation choice (documented in commit + DM):** the
wave-31 brief's literal wording "strip parscroll, cached output is
RENDERED backdrop, on hit single cache→window blit" would produce a
FROZEN PARALLAX visual regression on every non-BK_FIXED scrolltype
(the rendered backdrop output DEPENDS on parscroll for BK_PARALLAX /
BK_FOLLOWFG / BK_FASTLEFT — caching the rendered output and reusing
across parscroll changes means the backdrop visually freezes while
the camera moves). This patch implements the CORRECTNESS-PRESERVING
variant: cache the NATURAL-ORIGIN tiled output (parscroll-independent
contents) at dimensions large enough that the per-frame parscroll
can be applied as a src offset in the cache→window blit at hit time.
Same fps savings target (one blit on hit vs ~20 small tile blits on
miss for 64×64 bgs), no visual regression. See build-qa handoff DM
for the full reasoning + the cost-decomposition math.

**Cache structure:**
- New file-scope cache surface `g_backdrop_natural_sfc` separate from
  patch 0080's `g_backdrop_cache_sfc`. Sized
  `(screenWidth + bg_w) × (screenHeight + bg_h)` so any parscroll
  ∈ [0, bg_w) × [0, bg_h) produces an in-bounds src rect of size
  (screenWidth × screenHeight). For 64×64 bg at 320×240 screen,
  cache = 384×304 ≈ 117 KB.
- New key tuple: `(curmap, backdrop_id, scrolltype, indexed, w, h,
  format)` — no parscroll.
- New diagnostic counters: hits/misses/invalidates per block,
  emitted as `backdrop cache: engine-signaled invalidation,
  hit=N miss=M invalidate=K` once per audit-flush cadence (100 flips)
  via the new `map_emit_backdrop_natural_audit()` helper called from
  Renderer.cpp's `_maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit`.

**Dispatch order (in the generic-loop branch of map_draw_backdrop):**
1. Lever B (this patch) attempts first. On HIT: single src-offset
   blit cache→window (~3-4 ms); return. On MISS: realloc + tile-fill
   cache via `_render_natural_origin_to_cache` (~12-16 ms one-time
   per map change); blit cache→window; return.
2. On Lever B alloc/format/blit failure: fall through to patch 0080
   cache + wave-30 0126 thrashing-detect as safety net.
3. On all failures: fall through to legacy live tile loop (line 1080+).

**Scope:**
- Lever B applies ONLY to the GENERIC LOOP branch of map_draw_backdrop
  (the patch 0080 wrapper). Eligible scrolltypes per wave-29's
  scrolltype-vs-stage analysis: BK_FIXED (0), BK_PARALLAX (1),
  BK_FOLLOWFG (2), BK_FASTLEFT (5). Per stage.dat audit: 40 / 95
  stages = ~42% of game scenes engage Lever B (notable: Egg Corridor,
  Mimiga Village, Grasstown, Arthur's House, Sand Zone, all
  BK_PARALLAX).
- Lever B does NOT apply to BK_HIDE / BK_HIDE2 / BK_HIDE3
  scrolltypes (47 stages = ~50% — including Stage 12 First Cave,
  Stage 13 Start Point, Stage 18 Shelter). These return early at
  the BK_HIDE case with just a `Renderer::clearScreen(DK_BLUE)`.
  Lever B's path is never reached for these scenes; the backdrop
  cost remains the ~4 ms (or more on real HW) clearScreen call.
  **Wave-29's "First Cave heavy-music" 13.5 ms measurement may
  have been on a different stage (Mimiga Village or Egg Corridor —
  both BK_PARALLAX) than Stage 12. Operator's iter N+4 measurement
  must route through Lever-B-eligible scenes for the fps gain to
  materialize.**
- Lever B does NOT apply to BK_FASTLEFT_LAYERS / NOFALLLEFT (8
  stages — Outer Wall / Balcony / title menu). Those use the
  patch 0081 wrapper with 5-layer parscroll-dependent composition
  where each layer scrolls at a different speed; the composited
  output can't be expressed as a single src offset. Patch 0081
  branch keeps wave-30 thrashing-detect unchanged.

**Hypothesis savings** per wave-31 brief: -8 to -12 ms / flip in
heavy-music gameplay on Lever-B-eligible scenes. Replaces ~20 small
tile blits (~12-16 ms total for 64×64 bgs) on the wave-30 direct-to-
window path with a single 76 KB src-offset blit (~3-4 ms).

**On scenes that don't engage Lever B** (BK_HIDE2, BK_FASTLEFT_LAYERS,
etc.): 0 ms regression. Wave-30 thrashing-detect remains in place for
BK_FASTLEFT_LAYERS; BK_HIDE2 path is untouched.

Per `perf_predictions_unreliable.md` predictions on this project
have been 5-30× wrong; the savings depend on operator's scene route.
Could overshoot or undershoot the 40 fps target.

**Reuses existing `SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BACKDROP_CACHE=0` killswitch**
per team-lead direction — disables EVERYTHING (patch 0080 + wave-30
0126 + wave-31 0127). Cleanest semantics. No new env var.

**Fade-transition edge case:** team-lead's brief flagged this as in-
patch responsibility. Per code analysis: backdrop is not modulated
by per-pixel alpha — fade (`fade.Draw()`) and `tintScreen()` apply
to the whole window surface AFTER `map_draw_backdrop` returns,
overdrawing or darkening the backdrop's already-written pixels.
Caching the pre-fade backdrop is correct (fade reapplies to the
blitted output). No special-case gating needed.

**Strings marker:** LOG_INFO emitted unconditionally each audit-flush
(every 100 flips). flush-instr greps post-iter for `engine-signaled
invalidation, hit=N miss=M invalidate=K` to verify:
- hit/(hit+miss) ratio close to 1.0 in steady-state (cache hits
  every frame after the initial map-fill miss)
- invalidate count matches expected map-transition count
- per-block (n=100): expected ~99 hits + 1 miss per map entry, or
  100 hits steady-state

**Local DOSBox-X smoke** (this build, --fast, ~2 min):
- Title screen (BK_FASTLEFT_LAYERS): renders correctly; Lever B not
  engaged (patch 0081 wrapper, wave-30 thrashing-detect runs); 30+
  thrashing-detect markers observed.
- Intro cutscene + Start Point (BK_HIDE2 per stage.dat): renders
  correctly; Lever B not engaged (early-return at BK_HIDE case);
  Lever B counters show hit=0 miss=0 across all blocks. Expected.
- Shelter (Stage 18, BK_HIDE2): renders correctly; same as Start
  Point.
- Mimiga Village / Egg Corridor / other BK_PARALLAX scenes: not
  reached in local smoke (hold-key navigation pre-40fps is fiddly);
  build-qa real-HW iter validates Lever B engagement count via
  the marker.

**Risk profile:** structurally sound, follows existing patch 0080
pattern, killswitch tested. The only un-stress-tested element is
the src-offset blit correctness on BK_PARALLAX scenes — visual A/B
risk caught by build-qa's real-HW iter screenshot review.

Workspace-local; never upstreamed. See `docs/PHASE11-WAVE-30-FINDINGS.md`
§ 3 (wave-30 trajectory) + `docs/PHASE11-WAVE-29-HEADLINE.md` § 6
(Lever B original framing) for the wave-29 → wave-31 chain context.
